ok   an exact route is hit
ok   the handler sees the query
ok   the same path routes by method
ok   a path with a route for another method is 405
ok   a path nothing matched is the default 404
ok   the not-found handler can be replaced
ok   a static file is served with its type
ok   an unknown extension is octet-stream
ok   a missing file is 404
ok   a directory is 404
ok   the prefix alone is 404
ok   POST under the static prefix is 405
ok   the secret is served through its own prefix
ok   .. as a segment is refused
ok   .. deeper in is refused
ok   an empty segment is refused
ok   a backslash is refused
ok   a path not starting with / is refused
ok   ..x is a name, not a traversal
ok   a trailing slash on a route path is a different path
ok   a NUL byte in the path is refused
ok   httpPathSafe accepts a plain path
ok   httpPathSafe accepts a trailing slash
ok   httpPathSafe accepts the root
ok   httpPathSafe refuses the empty path
ok   httpPathSafe refuses /..
ok   httpPathSafe refuses a/../b
ok   httpPathSafe accepts a single dot segment
